"""Teamwork adapter — maps synaptory artifacts to Teamwork tasks/milestones/tags.

Mapping:
- Epic     -> Parent Task + `hc:epic` tag
- Story    -> Task + `hc:story` tag (child of epic task via parentTaskId)
- Task     -> Task + `hc:task` tag
- Bug      -> Task + `hc:bug` tag
- Sprint   -> Milestone (name: "Sprint N", deadline = sprint end date)
- Status   -> Task complete/uncomplete + `blocked` tag
- Priority -> Native task priority field (high, medium, low)
- Points   -> Tags (points:1, points:3, points:5, points:8)

ID convention:
  The Synaptory ID (e.g. US-037) is the canonical cross-adapter identifier.
  It is stored as a tag on each task for searchability.
  The Teamwork task ID (numeric) is an internal implementation detail.
  Task names use the clean human-readable name only — no ID prefix.
"""

